<p class="tk-prose__lead">In force since 6 October 2026. Third edition: adds the gallery, comments, groups and contacts, online visibility, device notifications, connection diagnostics and our own video intake.</p>

<h3>1. Who processes your data</h3>
<p>Personal data of Takebana users (takebana.com) is processed by Murat Kunizhev, Republic of Serbia. For questions about data and for requests about your rights, write to <a href="mailto:private@takebana.com">private@takebana.com</a>.</p>
<p>This policy follows the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), the Serbian Personal Data Protection Act, and the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA/CPRA).</p>

<h3>2. What we collect</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Account:</strong> email address, name and username, password stored as an irreversible hash, profile photo, “about me” text, the 18+ confirmation flag, the sign-in method (password or Google), your chosen language and theme, and your privacy settings.</li>
<li><strong>Content you create:</strong> streams and their settings, stream recordings, gallery photos and videos with captions and descriptions, cover images, comments, ratings, subscriptions, reports, stream chat messages.</li>
<li><strong>Messages:</strong> direct and group messages, attachments (photos, videos, voice messages, video notes, documents), forwarded posts and posts sent with “Share”, delivery and read marks, group members and their roles, and your contact list.</li>
<li><strong>Calls:</strong> who called whom, when, how long it lasted, how it ended and which route the connection took. We do not record or store the conversation itself.</li>
<li><strong>Online status:</strong> whether you are on the site right now and when you were last seen. You decide who sees this in your settings (section 7).</li>
<li><strong>Venues:</strong> name, type, country, city, address, map point, phone, email, opening hours, description, logo, photos, video menu, visitor ratings; when the venue camera was switched on and off.</li>
<li><strong>Device notifications:</strong> if you turn them on — the subscription address issued by your browser, encryption keys, language, browser name, and whether to show message text.</li>
<li><strong>Technical records:</strong> IP address and browser details in the activity log and the error log, times of sign-ins and actions; the email and address of failed sign-in attempts.</li>
<li><strong>Connection diagnostics:</strong> how an attempt to call, go live, watch a stream or camera, or upload or open a file went — its steps with timings, the result and the reason for a failure, network type, device and browser, time zone, and whether the site was opened from a home-screen icon. Added to this are the country and network provider, which our server looks up from the IP address in its own database without any outside request, and the address itself shortened to its network (for example, 203.0.113.0/24), which does not identify a person. We need this to find and fix failures with particular providers and countries.</li>
<li><strong>Visit statistics:</strong> which pages were opened, where visitors came from, how long they stayed, what they clicked, device type, browser, and approximate location by IP address. Collected by Yandex Metrica; details are in the <a href="/cookies">cookie notice</a>.</li>
</ul>
<p>We do not collect health data, beliefs, religion or other special categories of data, and we do not ask you for them. We have no advertising pixels and no cross-site tracking. Session recording (Webvisor) is off: what you type, including in messages, never reaches analytics.</p>

<h3>3. Why, and on what legal basis</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>To run the platform</strong> — sign-in, streams, calls, messages, the gallery, comments, venues, notifications. Basis: performance of our contract with you.</li>
<li><strong>Security and handling violations</strong> — activity and error logs, sign-in attempts, reports, account restrictions. Basis: our legitimate interest in protecting users and the platform.</li>
<li><strong>Keeping connections working for everyone</strong> — connection diagnostics. Basis: our legitimate interest; the data is reduced to the network level and deleted after 30 days.</li>
<li><strong>Service emails</strong> — email confirmation, email change, password recovery. Basis: performance of the contract.</li>
<li><strong>Understanding what people need on the site</strong> — visit statistics. Basis: your consent, which you give by continuing to use the site after the notice. You can withdraw it at any time — the <a href="/cookies">cookie notice</a> explains how; the site keeps working either way.</li>
<li><strong>Legal compliance</strong> — answering lawful requests from public authorities. Basis: legal obligation.</li>
</ul>
<p>We do not send marketing emails.</p>

<h3>4. Who receives data</h3>
<p>We do not sell data and do not pass it to advertisers. Data goes only to contractors the platform cannot run without:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Daily (Pluot Inc., USA)</strong> — video calling: calls and the host side of a stream from the browser. Receives your device address, and audio and video during the call or stream. When Daily is unreachable on your network, the call goes directly between devices or through our server, and Daily does not receive it.</li>
<li><strong>Bunny (BunnyWay d.o.o., Slovenia)</strong> — storage of stream recordings, gallery photos and videos and message attachments, and delivery of video from streams, recordings and venue cameras. Receives the viewer’s device address.</li>
<li><strong>Browser notification services</strong> (Google, Apple or Mozilla, depending on your browser) — deliver notifications if you turned them on. The notification content is encrypted with your device’s key; the service cannot read it.</li>
<li><strong>Google (Google Ireland Ltd.)</strong> — only Google sign-in, if you use it. We receive your email address and profile ID from Google.</li>
<li><strong>Resend (USA, sending from the São Paulo region, Brazil)</strong> — platform emails: email confirmation and change, password recovery. Receives your email address and the email text.</li>
<li><strong>Hostinger (Lithuania)</strong> — the server that runs the platform, holds the database and receives video from streams and venue cameras.</li>
<li><strong>Cloudflare (USA)</strong> — domain records and forwarding of mail sent to <code>@takebana.com</code> addresses to the platform’s working mailbox.</li>
<li><strong>Yandex (YANDEX LLC, Russia)</strong> — visit statistics through Yandex Metrica. Receives the data listed under “Visit statistics” in section 2 and the Metrica cookies.</li>
<li><strong>OpenStreetMap (Nominatim)</strong> — looking up coordinates for a venue address. Only the address text is sent, with no user data, and the request is made by our server, not by your browser.</li>
</ul>
<p>The venue map, fonts and the country lookup by IP run on our own server and send nothing outside.</p>
<p>Transfers outside the EU (Daily, Resend, Cloudflare, notification services) rely on the European Commission’s standard contractual clauses; transfers to Yandex rely on its data processing agreement. We also disclose data when lawfully required by a court or public authority, and we report child sexual exploitation material to law enforcement.</p>

<h3>5. Where data is stored</h3>
<p>The platform server and database are in the European Union. Stream recordings, the gallery and message attachments are kept in Bunny’s European storage. Database backups are kept on the same server.</p>

<h3>6. How long we keep it</h3>
<ul>
<li>The account and its content — for as long as the account exists.</li>
<li>Stream recordings, the gallery, messages and attachments — until the author deletes them or for as long as the account exists.</li>
<li>Disappearing messages — until the time the sender chose; unopened ones — 7 days.</li>
<li>Stream and venue camera chat messages — 90 days.</li>
<li>Notifications in the bell — 180 days.</li>
<li>Activity log (including IP address) — 180 days.</li>
<li>Error log — 90 days.</li>
<li>Connection diagnostics and venue camera records — 30 days.</li>
<li>Failed sign-in attempts — 1 day.</li>
<li>Sign-in session — 30 days from the last visit.</li>
<li>Password recovery link — 1 hour and a single use.</li>
</ul>
<p>Records are deleted automatically when their time runs out. When an account is deleted, the profile, streams, recordings, gallery, messages with attachments, calls, comments and ratings, subscriptions, contacts, venues and notification subscriptions are deleted at once. Earlier entries in the activity and error logs and in connection diagnostics remain until those records expire: they are needed in case of disputes and when handling violations.</p>

<h3>7. What other people see</h3>
<p>Your page is open to everyone: name, username, photo, description, gallery, stream recordings, number of subscribers. Viewers see live streams and venue cameras.</p>
<p>In your settings, under “Privacy”, you decide: who may message you, call you and add you to groups; who sees that you are online and who sees when you were last online (never wider than “online”); who may comment on your posts; and whether you appear in people search and author lists. You can also close your page and conversations to a particular person.</p>

<h3>8. Your rights</h3>
<p>You may: get a copy of your data; correct inaccurate data; delete data; restrict processing; object to processing based on our legitimate interest; receive your data in a machine-readable format; and withdraw consent where processing is based on consent.</p>
<p>Much of this you can do yourself: name, photo, description, privacy, language and theme in Settings; streams, recordings and the gallery on your own page; device notifications are turned off in Settings; and the whole account is deleted with the “Delete account” button in Settings.</p>
<p>For anything else, write to <a href="mailto:private@takebana.com">private@takebana.com</a>. We reply within 30 days. If you are not satisfied with our answer, you may complain to a data protection authority: in Serbia, the Commissioner for Information of Public Importance and Personal Data Protection; in the EU, the authority of your country.</p>

<h3>9. California residents</h3>
<p>Over the last 12 months we collected the categories of data listed in section 2: identifiers (email, name), device and connection information (IP address, browser, country and network provider), content you create, and information about your use of the platform. The source is you and your device. Purposes are in section 3.</p>
<p><strong>We do not sell personal information and do not share it for targeted advertising</strong> — for money or otherwise. We do not use sensitive information to infer characteristics about you.</p>
<p>You have the right to know what data we hold about you, to have it deleted or corrected, and not to be discriminated against for doing so. Send requests to the same address. An authorised agent may submit a request with proof of authority.</p>

<h3>10. Children</h3>
<p>The platform is intended for people over 18. We do not knowingly collect children’s data. If you know a child has created an account, write to us and we will delete the account and its data.</p>

<h3>11. Security</h3>
<p>Passwords are stored as an irreversible hash. The site runs over HTTPS. Device notifications are encrypted with the device’s key. Access to the server and database is limited to a small group of people. Administrator actions are logged. Still, no system is fully secure, and we cannot promise absolute security.</p>

<h3>12. Changes</h3>
<p>A new edition takes effect on the date shown at the top of this page. We will announce significant changes on the site.</p>
